<GARY-S> There are some strong opinions about what dpANS should be, and as it 
nears completion it is reasonable to see some incampments forming
<[doug] D.GARRETT> pmi, but in 25 words or less, what is dpANS ?
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> you want to splain it or should I gary?
<GARY-S> BASIS coming to fruition - is that too few ?
<[doug] D.GARRETT> oh, so this concerns Forth  (how do you get from Forth to 
"dp" ?)
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> dp = Draft Proposed, i.e. pre-standard
<[doug] D.GARRETT> ah, now I know.  Thank you.  25 words are up.  ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> draft proposed American National Standard
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> the X3 says we are in the computer languages group
<[doug] D.GARRETT> I've been amazed at all the smoke surrounding this ANSI 
bizness.  Much cooler-headed folk in MUMPS community...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> he must be having some kind of problem tonight
<GARY-S> Much noisier in the 'C' community
<[doug] D.GARRETT> we go thru new standardization every 3 years or so.
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> the smoke is just the normal process of a child growing up
<[doug] D.GARRETT> ah, thaz right, this is first time in the ANSI camp.
<GARY-S> X3J11 was _much_ nastier than X3J14
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> yes, the first is the worst, and now it is coming to a head
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> I expect it to get _real_ nasty now <sigh>
<[doug] D.GARRETT> Uh... could you explain to me (25 words or less, again)...
<[doug] D.GARRETT> how ANSI imprimateur will make life better for you at Forth 
Inc. ?
<GARY-S> I tend to fall into the Ridriguez/Petty/Wavrik camp, but try to stay 
neutral, or my message porting and SysOping would carry a stain.
<[doug] D.GARRETT> You, too, Gary.  What's it really mean for you, in real life?
<[doug] D.GARRETT> I'm curious, and don't know.  please ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> an ANS Forth standard would help FORTH, Inc. "sell" Forth 
to places that are concerned about using "standard" language
<GARY-S> It will legitimize Forth in DoD contract bids - that is certainly 
significant
<[doug] D.GARRETT> Very good reason!
<GARY-S> Hmm - echos of the same thought, Dennis
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> it is not just DOD, but other large corporations as well
<GARY-S> DoD is definitely the bell-cow, though.
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> we _have been_ turned down on jobs because we didn't use a 
"standard" language
<[doug] D.GARRETT> yeah.  Come to think of it, Veterans Admin couldn't 
"legally"...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> DOD does have some big contracts..that's for sure
<[doug] D.GARRETT> use MUMPS until ANSI kissed & blessed it.
<[doug] D.GARRETT> I assume there is an ANSI standard C, yes?
<GARY-S> Also, what happens in DoD carries BIG ripples throughout the rest of 
government. Witness Cobol. Witness Ada.
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> yes, C has made it, but they are also very bloody because 
of it
<GARY-S> That was the X3J11 I refered to earlier, Doug.
